From fed3e07fe19160464c35fb1488960c01132f56f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Feb 2024 04:32:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] pinctrl: add HiSilicon pinctrl framework

The HiSTB SoCs share a pinctrl block whose pins are muxed and configured
through a system-controller register window, and no mainline framework
covers it.

Add the generic part: the pin and function descriptions, the per-pin mux
application, and the three pinctrl ops structures. The ops are exported
and the file carries module metadata, because the SoC drivers sitting on
top are separate tristate objects that reference only the ops
structures, and every =m combination fails to link without them.

Signed-off-by: Yang Xiwen <forbidden405@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
